{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/speeches/amended-national-policy-statement-for-ports","content_id":"339a690a-97f7-4a61-8bb9-cce4215a67a4","description":"Announcing the laying before Parliament of the final proposed text of the amended national policy statement for ports.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Development of ports in England, as in other parts of the United Kingdom, is essential for supporting growth, energy resilience and energy transition. It is equally important that this development should take place with consideration for the environment, and that port facilities should be well designed with both those ends in mind.</p>\n\n<p>The National Policy Statement for Ports (<abbr title=\"National Policy Statement for Ports\">NPSP</abbr>), which applies to England, and in Wales, to the reserved trust port, Milford Haven, sets the policy framework for decisions on nationally significant infrastructure in the sector.</p>\n\n<p>It continues the long-standing policy of enabling our competitive ports sector to respond in an agile manner to rapidly evolving market demands, using the department’s port freight demand forecasts (which we published alongside our consultation) as a yardstick but not as a constraint on local commercial judgements. It also updates the policy in detail to reflect the wider present institutional and regulatory framework and the government’s priorities.</p>\n\n<p>I am grateful to everyone who responded to <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/consultations/proposed-amendments-to-the-existing-national-policy-statement-for-ports\">the consultation on earlier drafts</a>, and to the Transport Committee for its thorough scrutiny of the proposals.</p>\n\n<p>Following that consultation and scrutiny, I am today, pursuant to section 9(5) Planning Act 2008, presenting a response to the <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm5901/cmselect/cmtrans/1028/report.html\">Transport Committee’s Report (HC 1028)</a> on its scrutiny and to the consultation, and pursuant to section 9(8), laying before Parliament the final proposed text of <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-national-policy-statement-for-ports\">the amended national policy statement</a> for the prescribed consideration period of 21 sitting days.</p>\n\n<p>Copies of these documents will be made available in the libraries of both Houses and on the department’s website, where a post-adoption statement will also be published in due course.</p>\n\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-06T11:18:24Z"}],"delivered_on":"2026-07-06T10:00:00+01:00","first_public_at":"2026-07-06T12:18:24.000+01:00","image":{"alt_text":"Keir Mather MP","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/668ea1a0fc8e12ac3edafa82/Keir-Mather.jpg"},"location":"Houses of Parliament","political":true},"document_type":"written_statement","first_published_at":"2026-07-06T12:18:24+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/speeches/amended-national-policy-statement-for-ports","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/speeches/amended-national-policy-statement-for-ports","base_path":"/government/speeches/amended-national-policy-statement-for-ports","content_id":"339a690a-97f7-4a61-8bb9-cce4215a67a4","document_type":"written_statement","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-06T11:18:24Z","schema_name":"speech","title":"Amended national policy statement for ports","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/amended-national-policy-statement-for-ports","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D9","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-transport","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-transport","base_path":"/government/organisations/department-for-transport","content_id":"4c717efc-f47b-478e-a76d-ce1ae0af1946","details":{"acronym":"DfT","brand":"department-for-transport","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/654bbccfe2e16a000d42abe1/s960_dft-gmh-960.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/654bbccfe70413000dfc4a51/s300_dft-gmh-960.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department<br/>for Transport"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Transport","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-transport","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/keir-mather","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/keir-mather","base_path":"/government/people/keir-mather","content_id":"6cfb87fe-5a4c-46e1-acf7-7a57e17a1adf","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-09-08T07:07:02Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Keir Mather MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/keir-mather","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D9","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-transport","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/department-for-transport","base_path":"/government/organisations/department-for-transport","content_id":"4c717efc-f47b-478e-a76d-ce1ae0af1946","details":{"acronym":"DfT","brand":"department-for-transport","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/654bbccfe2e16a000d42abe1/s960_dft-gmh-960.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/654bbccfe70413000dfc4a51/s300_dft-gmh-960.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Department<br/>for Transport"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Department for Transport","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/department-for-transport","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--300","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--300","base_path":"/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--300","content_id":"f24f02f6-57a8-41f5-bf40-584fb798cad1","details":{"body":"<p>The Minister for Aviation, Maritime and Decarbonisation is responsible for:   </p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>aviation and airport expansion </li>\n  <li>maritime </li>\n  <li>decarbonisation and electric vehicles (<abbr title=\"electric vehicles\">EVs</abbr>) </li>\n  <li>freight and borders </li>\n  <li>international</li>\n  <li>security</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/parliamentary-under-secretary-of-state--343\">Minister for Aviation, Maritime and Logistics</a> replaced this role on 22 July 2026.</p>\n\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-08-19T13:42:09Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Parliamentary Under-Secretary of State (Minister for Aviation, Maritime and Decarbonisation) ","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/parliamentary-un